A||||4||jelly2m8||T-Top disassembly question||||1||
Z||000000||jelly2m8||12-10-2001||07:48 PM||||Anybody know how to remove the outer roof mouldings at the back of the glass panels on a T-Top?<P> Looked at the waterleak manual, nothing specific of removing these. Althought it looks like it might have tabs that engage the steel roof panel underneath. My guess would be to pull them ahead?<P>Also, the trim caps on the glass itself that covers the latch mechanism. According to the water leak manual, all you need to do is remove the 2 screws, and pull the trimm off with the latch in the open position. Tried that, no dice. Doesn't seem to be near enough clearance that way.<P>Thanks<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Tina||12-10-2001||08:55 PM||||As far as I remember (the outer roof mouldings) top one is glued down, bottom one is the one with the screws.<BR>As to the caps, you really gotta fight with them a little, but they <B>Do</B> come off.<BR>Make sure you do it somewhere warm though, you don't want the plastic to crack trying to <BR>fight it off.<P>Tina<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||jelly2m8||12-10-2001||10:07 PM||||Thanks Tina,<P> I'll give it a go in the morning.<P>Ya, I gotta be extra careful with the plastic trim, the trim on this car is real brittle, the Florida sun hasen't been kind to it ovewr the years.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||12-10-2001||10:45 PM||||The black plastic trim at the rear edge of the glass, that fills in the gap between the glass and the front edge of the rear clip...<P>There should be 3 or 4 rivets on each side, that go through the P-seal (the fuzzy fabric), and the black plastic trim, into the steel structure. Sometimes the P-seal is installed *over* the rivets.<BR>Once you remove the rivets, the main thing holding the black trim in place is whatever adhesive the assembler used. Usually it's butyl rubber or silicone. There are also probably some metal clips (hooks?) on the bottom edge of the back of the trim. The metal clips hook under the front edge of the rear clip. This front edge is actually about 3/8 - 1/2 inch wide, and extends under the back edge of the black molding. Be careful removing the moldings. They *will* break. Been there. Done that. Might help to squeeze a knife between the *front* of the trim and the steel structure to cut the adhesive.<P>Fieroparts.com used to have replacements. Not sure, now. <P>The caps over the latch assembly *do* come off. You'll swear you're going to break them, but it can be done.<P>Good luck.  <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 12-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||jelly2m8||12-10-2001||10:58 PM||||Cool, thanks Raydar. I drilled the heads off of the rivets to get the p-seals off, I'll drill the rivet right out and give that a try.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg"> ||||reg||1
